< {"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"reasoning","id":"deepseek_reasoning","summary":[],"content":["Now I have a complete picture of Round 1. Let me plan the Round 2 changes:\n\n1. **Remove external network dependencies**: Remove Google Fonts links from index.html, add local font stack to CSS.\n2. **Add Next Best Actions queue**: A new section that derives actionable tasks from the data across all 5 domains.\n3. **Add Risk Playbook/Report section**: For high-risk accounts, show recommended actions, owner, due date, impact amount.\n4. **Add more interactions**: \n   - Owner/status filter on actions\n   - Action completion/deferral with state changes\n   - Report tab switching (Dashboard vs Playbook vs Actions)\n   - Export text capability\n5. **Create REPORT.md** documenting the 2-round smoke benchmark\n6. **Extend validate.mjs** with new checks\n7. **Run npm test, fix issues**\n\nLet me think about the architecture:\n\n- I need a tabbed interface: Dashboard | Actions | Playbook\n- The Actions tab shows a queue of tasks derived from the data\n- The Playbook tab shows high-risk accounts with recommended actions\n- Both need new rendering functions\n\nFor the data model extension, I'll add a `playbook` data structure in data.js that maps risk patterns to recommended actions, and an `actions` queue derived from current data.\n\nLet me think about the actions model:\n- Each action has: id, accountId, domain, type, description, owner, dueDate, impact (amount), status (pending/completed/deferred)\n- Actions are derived from: at-risk renewals → schedule exec call; overdue invoices → send payment reminder; P1 tickets → escalate; usage drop → schedule check-in; active incidents → post status update\n\nFor the playbook, I'll add predefined playbook entries for different risk patterns.\n\nLet me start with the changes:\n\n1. First, update index.html: remove Google Fonts, add tab navigation, add new sections\n2. Update data.js: add actions and playbook data structures\n3. Update components.js: add rendering for actions, playbook, tabs\n4. Update app.js: add tab switching, action state management, export\n5. Update styles.css: add new styles for tabs, actions, playbook\n6. Create REPORT.md\n7. Update validate.mjs\n\nLet me be careful about not making files too large. I'll keep data.js under control and add new rendering functions to components.js.\n\nLet me start coding all of this.\n\nFor the offline fonts - I need to replace the Google Fonts with a system font stack that looks good. The CSS already has `--font: 'Inter', -apple-system, ...` so I can just set it to system fonts and it will still look decent. The Inter font won't be available offline, but system sans-serif will fallback gracefully.\n\nActually, let me also add a `public/report.html` that's a simple accessible report page. Wait, the requirement says `public/report.html` or `REPORT.md`. A REPORT.md at the root makes more sense as it's lightweight and doesn't need to be served. Let me do REPORT.md.\n\nLet me now implement all changes. I'll work through each file systematically."]},"threadId":"019e2fa3-65fc-7381-a85d-304bffcc8f7b","turnId":"019e2fb1-9f6e-7273-a314-e345c1e5ec4f","completedAtMs":1778916688354}}
