< {"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"reasoning","id":"deepseek_reasoning","summary":[],"content":["Good. Now let me build the major new features. I'll start with extending data.js to add the playbook and actions data structures, then update components.js with new rendering functions, then update app.js with new interactions, then update index.html with tabs, then update CSS.\n\nLet me plan the data additions:\n\n1. **Playbook entries**: predefined risk-response playbooks keyed by risk patterns\n2. **Actions queue**: a computed list of concrete tasks derived from the data\n\nFor playbooks:\n```js\nconst playbooks = [\n  { id: 'pb-001', pattern: 'renewal_critical', title: 'Executive Save Play', \n    steps: ['Schedule exec-to-exec call within 48h', 'Prepare retention offer', 'Escalate to VP Customer Success'],\n    trigger: 'Renewal status is Critical' },\n  ...\n];\n```\n\nFor actions, I'll compute them from existing data rather than hardcoding them. Each action references a source (renewal, invoice, ticket, etc.) and has a status.\n\nLet me also think about the \"owner\" filter - I need to add owner assignments to actions. The CSM from accounts is a natural owner.\n\nLet me write the extended data.js now. I need to add:\n- `actions` array (derived/computed from other data)\n- `playbooks` array\n- `getActions()` function\n- `getPlaybookForAccount(acctId)` function\n\nThen in components.js I'll add:\n- `renderActionsQueue(actions, filter)` - the actions tab content\n- `renderPlaybook(accountId)` - the playbook tab content\n- `renderTabs(activeTab)` - tab bar\n- `renderExportText(data)` - text export\n\nThen in app.js I'll add:\n- Tab switching state\n- Action status mutation (complete/defer)\n- Owner filter\n- Export trigger\n\nLet me start building."]},"threadId":"019e2fa3-65fc-7381-a85d-304bffcc8f7b","turnId":"019e2fb1-9f6e-7273-a314-e345c1e5ec4f","completedAtMs":1778916758337}}
